st_replay_aborts_and_drifts_on_illegal_hop assert that a failed replay hop raises RuntimeError (acli) OR urllib.error.HTTPError/JiraAPIError, but the Data Center transport's transition_issue_by_name raises ValueError (not RuntimeError) when no transition reaches the target.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe6467c296c5c5d2a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section 3 / AC 'test_replay_aborts_and_drifts_on_illegal_hop'","norm_id":"n2c94afc80478db57","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reconciling against a Jira Data Center instance where a recorded intermediate hop is illegal from the issue's current workflow state"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Broaden the abort catch to (RuntimeError, ValueError, HTTPError, JiraAPIError), or catch a common base, and update the AC to exercise both a RuntimeError (acli) and a ValueError (DC) mid-chain hop.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the current-Jira-status-to-hop-index resolution handles the non-injective LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA (e.g. match on the Jira name directly against the mapped hop list rather than inverting to a single rebar status).","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'map fields.status.name back to a rebar status via the inverse of LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA, find its index in the recorded hop list'","value_maps.py:78-86 LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA maps multiple locals to one Jira name: 'in_progress' and 'blocked' both -> 'In Progress'; 'closed','cancelled','deleted' all -> 'Done'","A many-to-one map has no unique inverse, so 'In Progress' or 'Done' cannot be resolved to a single rebar status by simple inversion"],"finding":"Section 2 relies on mapping the current Jira status back to a rebar status via 'the inverse of LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA', but that map is not injective, so a well-defined inverse does not exist.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe3d7958b4bae656e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section 2 ('map fields.status.name back to a rebar status via the inverse of LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA')","norm_id":"n442353fa039454b4","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Computing the resume index when get_issue reports 'In Progress' or 'Done' and the recorded hop list distinguishes in_progress/blocked or closed/cancelled/deleted"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Compute the resume index by mapping each recorded hop local->Jira name and matching the get_issue Jira name against that already-mapped list (last matching index), avoiding any need to invert the map.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Resolve the current-status match in Jira-name space (compare get_issue's fields.status.name against each recorded hop's forward LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA mapping) rather than inverting the non-injective map back to a single rebar status.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["value_maps.py:78-86: {'closed':'Done','cancelled':'Done','deleted':'Done','in_progress':'In Progress','blocked':'In Progress'}","Plan: 'map fields.status.name back to a rebar status via the inverse of LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA, find its index in the recorded hop list'"],"finding":"Step 2 maps the current Jira status back to a rebar status via 'the inverse of LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA', but that map is non-injective: 'In Progress' has preimages {in_progress, blocked} and 'Done' has {closed, cancelled, deleted} (value_maps.py:78-86). An inverse lookup is therefore ambiguous and can pick the wrong local status, mislocating the resume index in the hop list.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb8dee7d345d9fc4d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2","norm_id":"nf8f827cd24dffe28","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Recorded hops include a 'blocked' (->'In Progress') hop and get_issue reports 'In Progress'; the inverse arbitrarily resolves to 'in_progress' vs 'blocked' and lands on the wrong index."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Compute the Jira-name hop list once (forward-map each recorded local status), then find the current Jira status by name equality in that list and replay the suffix — never invert the map.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add `ValueError` (specifically `jira_datacenter.transitions.IllegalTransitionError`) to the replay abort-on-raise set alongside RuntimeError/HTTPError/JiraAPIError, since the DataCenter transport signals an unreachable transition with a ValueError subclass, not RuntimeError/HTTPError.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 3: 'if ANY replay hop raises — RuntimeError (no transition reaches; acli.py:536) OR urllib.error.HTTPError/JiraAPIError ... abort replay'","adapters/jira_datacenter/transitions.py:33 `class IllegalTransitionError(ValueError)` — 'Deliberately not an HTTPError subclass'; docstring: 'Subclasses ValueError so it stays compatible with callers already catching the ValueError resolve_transition raises for an unreachable state'","adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py:236 transition_issue_by_name docstring: 'Raises ValueError when no transition reaches the requested state — the error type callers already expect'","adapters/jira/acli.py:535 raises RuntimeError — the two implementors signal the same failure with different exception types"],"finding":"The plan's replay abort logic catches RuntimeError / HTTPError / JiraAPIError as the 'no transition reaches' signal, but the DataCenter transport (one of the two named transition_issue_by_name implementors) raises IllegalTransitionError, a ValueError subclass that is deliberately NOT an HTTPError. On the DC backend a mid-chain illegal hop escapes replay unhandled instead of aborting to comment-fallback + drift.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc661935b5cca54e2","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 (failure mode); AC test_replay_aborts_and_drifts_on_illegal_hop","norm_id":"ncdbef9c9cf53f37f","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A DataCenter-backed reconcile hits a mid-chain hop the workflow forbids; transition_issue_by_name raises IllegalTransitionError(ValueError), which the replay's except clause does not name, so it propagates instead of falling through to comment-fallback + drift."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In replay_transition, catch (RuntimeError, ValueError, urllib.error.HTTPError, JiraAPIError) — or the shared IllegalTransitionError base — so both the ACLI (RuntimeError) and DataCenter (IllegalTransitionError/ValueError) implementors of transition_issue_by_name route to the same abort-to-drift path; add a DC-transport-shaped test case.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify how cyclic/repeated STATUS histories are handled — e.g. match the LAST occurrence of the current status (or collapse to the terminal target) so replay only ever moves forward.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["txn.py appends one STATUS event per transition (txn.py:330-336) with no de-duplication, so repeated statuses accumulate in filename order","Plan: 'find its index in the recorded hop list, and replay only the hops AFTER it'"],"finding":"Step 2 does 'find its index in the recorded hop list' but rebar's STATUS history is a full append-only event log that can legitimately cycle (e.g. open->in_progress->open->in_progress->closed). A first-occurrence index search over such a list can resume at an earlier point and replay backward or duplicate hops; the plan does not specify using the LAST occurrence or otherwise handling cyclic histories.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8116c330405f54dd","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2","norm_id":"n92d67fa3e4a6bf4f","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A ticket reopened then re-closed produces [open, in_progress, open, in_progress, closed]; matching current status 'In Progress' at its FIRST index replays a stale open->... tail."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that replay logs the attempted hop sequence, the current-status resume point, and the aborting hop/exception before falling through to drift.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'abort replay and fall through to the EXISTING comment-fallback + drift arm ... exactly as today'","No mention of a log line distinguishing 'replay attempted N hops then aborted' from 'direct transition failed'"],"finding":"The plan does not specify any logging/metric/trace for the replay attemp